NumericalAlgebraicGeometry -- Numerical Algebraic Geometry
**********************************************************

Description
===========

The package *note NumericalAlgebraicGeometry: Top,, also known as NAG4M2
(Numerical Algebraic Geometry for Macaulay2), implements methods of polynomial
homotopy continuation to solve systems of polynomial equations,
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = CC[x,y,z];                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : F = {x^2+y^2+z^2-1, y-x^2, z-x^3};                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : s = solveSystem F                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = {{-.540536-1.03152*ii, -.771845+1.11514*ii, 1.5675+.193395*ii},         |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     {-.540536+1.03152*ii, -.771845-1.11514*ii, 1.5675-.193395*ii},          |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     {-.737353, .543689, -.400891}, {.540536-1.03152*ii, -.771845-1.11514*ii,|
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     -1.5675+.193395*ii}, {.540536+1.03152*ii, -.771845+1.11514*ii,          |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     -1.5675-.193395*ii}, {.737353, .543689, .400891}}                       |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : realPoints s                                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = {{-.737353, .543689, -.400891}, {.737353, .543689, .400891}}            |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
and describe positive-dimensional complex algebraic varieties, 
+---------------------------------------------+
|i5 : R = CC[x,y,z];                          |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i6 : sph = x^2+y^2+z^2-1;                    |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i7 : I = ideal {x*sph*(y-x^2), sph*(z-x^3)}; |
|                                             |
|o7 : Ideal of R                              |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i8 : numericalIrreducibleDecomposition I     |
|                                             |
|o8 = a "numerical variety" with components in|
|     dim 1:  (dim=1,deg=1) (dim=1,deg=3)     |
|     dim 2:  (dim=2,deg=2)                   |
|                                             |
|o8 : NumericalVariety                        |
+---------------------------------------------+

Basic types (such as *note Point: (NAGtypes)AbstractPoint, and *note
WitnessSet: (NAGtypes)WitnessSet,) are defined in the package *note NAGtypes:
(NAGtypes)Top,.

Basic functions:
----------------

  * *note track: track_lpList_cmList_cmList_rp, -- track a linear segment
    homotopy given start and target system
  * *note solveSystem: solveSystem_lpList_rp, -- solve a system of polynomial
    equations
  * *note refine: refine_lpList_cmList_rp, -- refine numerical solutions to a
    system of polynomial equations
  * *note totalDegreeStartSystem: totalDegreeStartSystem_lpList_rp, --
    construct a start system for the total degree homotopy
  * *note numericalIrreducibleDecomposition:
    numericalIrreducibleDecomposition_lpIdeal_rp, -- constructs a numerical
    variety defined by the given ideal
  * *note sample: sample_lpWitnessSet_rp, -- sample a point on a component
  * isSubset(NumericalVariety,NumericalVariety) (missing documentation)
Optionally, the user may outsource some basic routines to *note Bertini:
(Bertini)Top, and *note PHCpack: (PHCpack)Top, (look for *note Software:
Software, option).

Service functions:
------------------

  * Many service functions (such as *note areEqual: (NAGtypes)areEqual, and
    *note sortSolutions: (NAGtypes)sortSolutions_lpList_rp,) are defined in the
    package *note NAGtypes: (NAGtypes)Top,.
  * *note setDefault: setDefault, -- set/get the default parameters for
    continuation algorithms
  * *note getDefault: setDefault, -- set/get the default parameters for
    continuation algorithms
  * *note NAGtrace: NAGtrace_lpZZ_rp, -- set the trace level in
    NumericalAlgebraicGeometry package
  * *note newton: newton, -- Newton-Raphson method
  * *note isOn: isOn, -- determines if a point belongs to a variety
  * *note union: (Macaulay2Doc)union, -- compute the union
  * *note removeRedundantComponents:
    removeRedundantComponents_lpNumericalVariety_rp, -- remove redundant
    components

Functions related to *note Certified: Certified, tracking:
----------------------------------------------------------

  * *note randomInitialPair: randomInitialPair, -- a random initial pair
  * *note goodInitialPair: goodInitialPair_lpList_rp, -- make an initial pair
    conjectured to be good by Shub and Smale
  * *note randomSd: randomSd_lpList_rp, -- a random homogeneous system of
    polynomial equations

References:
-----------

  * A.J. Sommese, J. Verschelde, and C.W. Wampler, "Introduction to numerical
    algebraic geometry", in "Solving polynomial equations" (2005), 301--338
  * A.J. Sommese and C.W. Wampler, "The numerical solution of systems of
    polynomials", World Scientific Publishing (2005)
  * C. Beltran and A. Leykin, "Certified numerical homotopy tracking",
    Experimental Mathematics 21(1): 69-83 (2012)
  * R. Krone and A. Leykin, "Numerical algorithms for detecting embedded
    components.", arXiv:1405.7871

