Certified -- a value for the option Predictor that triggers certified tracking
******************************************************************************

Description
===========

Tells basic functions, e.g., *note track: track_lpList_cmList_cmList_rp,, to
use soft certification described in

C. Beltran and A. Leykin, "Certified numerical homotopy tracking", Experimental
Mathematics 21(1): 69-83 (2012)

The code for robust certification is not incorporated in this package at the
moment; the location of this stand-alone code is in the references of

C. Beltran and A. Leykin, "Robust certified numerical homotopy tracking",
Foundations of Computational Mathematics 13(2): 253-295 (2013)

The functions related to this paper are:

  * *note randomInitialPair: randomInitialPair, -- a random initial pair
  * *note goodInitialPair: goodInitialPair_lpList_rp, -- make an initial pair
    conjectured to be good by Shub and Smale
  * *note randomSd: randomSd_lpList_rp, -- a random homogeneous system of
    polynomial equations
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = CC[x,y,z];                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : S = {x^2-z^2,y^2-z^2};                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : T = {x^2+y^2-z^2, x*y};                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : solsS = {(1,-1,1),(1,1,1)};                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : track(S,T,solsS,Predictor=>Certified,Normalize=>true)             |
|                                                                       |
|o5 = {{.00000107266, -.70712, .70712}, {.707125, -1.48993e-7, .707107}}|
|                                                                       |
|o5 : List                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+

