endGameCauchy -- Cauchy end game for getting a better approximation of a singular solution
******************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        endGameCauchy(H,t'end,p0)
        endGameCauchy(H,t'end,points)
  * Inputs:
      * H, an instance of the type *note GateHomotopy:
        gateHomotopy_lpGateMatrix_cmGateMatrix_cmInputGate_rp,,
      * t'end, a *note number: (Macaulay2Doc)Number,, 
      * p0, a *note point: (NAGtypes)AbstractPoint,, 
      * points, a *note mutable matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)MutableMatrix,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * backtrack factor
      * *note CorrectorTolerance: numerical homotopy tracking options, => ...,
        default value null, options for core functions of Numerical Algebraic
        Geometry
      * *note EndZoneFactor: numerical homotopy tracking options, => ...,
        default value null, options for core functions of Numerical Algebraic
        Geometry
      * *note InfinityThreshold: numerical homotopy tracking options, => ...,
        default value null, options for core functions of Numerical Algebraic
        Geometry
      * *note maxCorrSteps: numerical homotopy tracking options, => ...,
        default value null, options for core functions of Numerical Algebraic
        Geometry
      * number of vertices
      * *note numberSuccessesBeforeIncrease: numerical homotopy tracking
        options, => ..., default value null, options for core functions of
        Numerical Algebraic Geometry
      * *note stepIncreaseFactor: numerical homotopy tracking options, => ...,
        default value null, options for core functions of Numerical Algebraic
        Geometry
      * *note tStep: numerical homotopy tracking options, => ..., default value
        null, options for core functions of Numerical Algebraic Geometry
      * *note tStepMin: numerical homotopy tracking options, => ..., default
        value null, options for core functions of Numerical Algebraic Geometry

Description
===========

Refines an approximation of a (singular) solution to a polynomial system which
was obtained via homotopy continuation. This method is used for posprocessing
in the blackbox solver implemented in *note solveSystem:
solveSystem_lpList_rp,.

+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : CC[x,y]                                                      |
|                                                                  |
|o1 = CC  [x..y]                                                   |
|       53                                                         |
|                                                                  |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                               |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : T = {(x-2)^3,y-x+x^2-x^3}                                    |
|                                                                  |
|       3     2               3    2                               |
|o2 = {x  - 6x  + 12x - 8, - x  + x  - x + y}                      |
|                                                                  |
|o2 : List                                                         |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : sols = solveSystem(T,PostProcess=>false);                    |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : p0 = first sols;                                             |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : peek p0                                                      |
|                                                                  |
|o5 = Point{cache => CacheTable{...5...}                          }|
|           Coordinates => {2.005+.016802*ii, -381.636-1080.53*ii} |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : t'end = 1                                                    |
|                                                                  |
|o6 = 1                                                            |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : p = endGameCauchy(p0.cache#"H",t'end,p0)                     |
|                                                                  |
|o7 = p                                                            |
|                                                                  |
|o7 : Point                                                        |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note refine: refine_lpList_cmList_rp, -- refine numerical solutions to a
    system of polynomial equations

