GateSystem -- a system of functions evaluated via a straightline program
************************************************************************

Description
===========

An object of this type is a system of functions evaluated via an SLP that is
constructed using the tools of package *note SLPexpressions:
(SLPexpressions)Top,.

An object of this type (constructed with *note gateSystem: gateSystem,) is a
*note System: (NAGtypes)System, of functions represented via a *note
GateMatrix: (SLPexpressions)GateMatrix,. In particular, polynomial systems and
systems of rational functions can be represented this way.

Unlike *note PolySystem: (NAGtypes)PolySystem,, the functions of a *note
GateSystem: GateSystem, do not belong to a ring and can be evaluated on *note
Number: (Macaulay2Doc)Number,s and *note RingElement:
(Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,s as long as the constants in the evaluation circuits
can be promoted to the corresponding *note Ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,s.

