      * GeneralPosition => ..., default value false, make a random unitary
        change of coordinates
  * Outputs:
      * S, contains homogeneous polynomials
      * sol, contains one solution of S

Description
===========

Generates a start system S that is conjectured to have good complexity when
used in linear homotopy with target system T leading to one solution. For more
details see: C. Beltran and A. Leykin, "Certified numerical homotopy tracking",
Experimental Mathematics 21(1): 69-83 (2012)


+--------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : T = randomSd {2,3};                                            |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : (S,solsS) = goodInitialPair T                                  |
|                                                                    |
|                                 2                                  |
|o2 = ({1.41421x1*x3, 1.73205x2*x3 }, {{0, 0, 1}})                   |
|                                                                    |
|o2 : Sequence                                                       |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : M = track(S,T,solsS,gamma=>0.6+0.8*ii,Software=>M2)            |
|                                                                    |
|o3 = {{.751732+.463283*ii, .284351-.0717164*ii, .348144-.114302*ii}}|
|                                                                    |
|o3 : List                                                           |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------+

