numerical homotopy tracking options -- options for core functions of Numerical Algebraic Geometry
*************************************************************************************************

  * [gamma]:  (default gamma = 1). A parameter in the homotopy:
    H(t)=(1-t)^{tDegree} S + \gamma t^{tDegree} T.
  * [tDegree]:  (default tDegree = 1). A parameter in the homotopy:
    H(t)=(1-t)^{tDegree} S + \gamma t^{tDegree} T.
  * [tStep]:  (default tStep = .05). Initial step size.
  * [tStepMin]:  (default tStepMin = .000001). Minimal step size.
  * [stepIncreaseFactor]:  (default stepIncreaseFactor = 2). Determines how the
    step size is adjusted.
  * [numberSuccessesBeforeIncrease]:  (default numberSuccessesBeforeIncrease =
    4). Determines how the step size is adjusted.
  * [Predictor]:  (default Predictor = RungeKutta4). A method to predict the
    next point on the homotopy path: choose between *note RungeKutta4:
    numerical homotopy tracking options,, *note Tangent: numerical homotopy
    tracking options,, *note Euler: numerical homotopy tracking options,, *note
    Secant: numerical homotopy tracking options,, *note Multistep: numerical
    homotopy tracking options,, *note Certified: Certified,. The option *note
    Certified: Certified, provides certified tracking.
  * [MultistepDegree]:  (default MultistepDegree = 3). Degree of the Multistep
    predictor.
  * [maxCorrSteps]:  (default maxCorrSteps = 3). Max number of steps corrector
    takes before a failure is declared.
  * [CorrectorTolerance]:  (default CorrectorTolerance = .000001). Corrector
    succeeds if the relative error does not exceed this tolerance.
  * [EndZoneFactor]:  (default EndZoneFactor = .05). Determines the size of the
    "end zone", the interval at the end of the path where *note
    CorrectorTolerance: numerical homotopy tracking options, is tighter.
  * [InfinityThreshold]:  (default InfinityThreshold = 1e9). Paths are
    truncated if the norm of the approximation exceeds the threshold.
  * [Projectivize]:  (default Projectivize = false). If true then the system is
    homogenized and the projective tracker is executed.
  * [Normalize]:  (default Normalize = false). Normalize the start and target
    systems w.r.t. the Bombieri-Weyl norm.
  * [NoOutput]:  (default NoOutput = false). If true, no output is produced
    (used by developers).
  * [Iterations]:  (default Iterations = 30). Number of refining iterations of
    Newton's method.
  * [Bits]:  (default Bits = infinity). Number of bits of precision.
  * [ErrorTolerance]:  (default ErrorTolerance = 1e-8). A bound on the desired
    estimated error.
  * [ResidualTolerance]:  (default ResidualTolerance = .0001). A bound on
    desired residual.
  * [Precision]:  (default Precision = 53). Precision of the floating-point
    numbers used in computation. If set to *note infinity:
    (Macaulay2Doc)infinity,(EXPERIMENTAL!) the precision in homotopy
    continuation adapts according to numerical conditioning. The default
    setting, DoublePrecision, forces fast arithmetic and linear algebra in
    standard precision. (Other settings invoke MPFR library.)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

