regeneration(List) -- solve a system of polynomial equations with regeneration method
*************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note regeneration: regeneration_lpList_rp,
  * Usage: 
        Ws = regeneration F
  * Inputs:
      * F, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, contains polynomials with complex
        coefficients
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Output => ..., default value Singular
      * *note Software: Software, => ..., default value null, specify internal
        or external software
  * Outputs:
      * Ws, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, contains *note witness sets:
        (NAGtypes)WitnessSet, for equidimensional components of the variety
        {x|F(x)=0}

Description
===========

Regeneration is a blackbox method that obtains a numerical description of an
algebraic variety. Note that Ws are not necessarily irreducible witness sets;
use *note decompose(WitnessSet): decompose_lpWitnessSet_rp, to decompose into
irreducibles.
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = CC[x,y]                                        |
|                                                        |
|o1 = R                                                  |
|                                                        |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                     |
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : F = {x^2+y^2-1, x*y};                              |
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : regeneration F                                     |
|                                                        |
|o3 = a "numerical variety" with components in           |
|     dim 0:  [dim=0,deg=4]-*may be reducible*-          |
|                                                        |
|o3 : NumericalVariety                                   |
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : R = CC[x,y,z]                                      |
|                                                        |
|o4 = R                                                  |
|                                                        |
|o4 : PolynomialRing                                     |
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : sph = (x^2+y^2+z^2-1);                             |
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : regeneration {sph*(x-1)*(y-x^2), sph*(y-2)*(z-x^3)}|
|                                                        |
|o6 = a "numerical variety" with components in           |
|     dim 1:  [dim=1,deg=7]-*may be reducible*-          |
|     dim 2:  [dim=2,deg=2]-*may be reducible*-          |
|                                                        |
|o6 : NumericalVariety                                   |
+--------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

This function is under development. It may not work well if the input
represents a nonreduced scheme.The (temporary) option *note Output:
regeneration_lpList_rp, can take two values: *note Regular:
(NAGtypes)AbstractPoint, (default) and *note Singular:
(NAGtypes)AbstractPoint,. It specifies whether the algorithm attempts to keep
singular points.

See also
========

  * decompose(WitnessSet) (missing documentation)

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note regeneration(List): regeneration_lpList_rp, -- solve a system of
    polynomial equations with regeneration method
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

