solveSystem(List) -- solve a system of polynomial equations
***********************************************************

  * Function: *note solveSystem: solveSystem_lpList_rp,
  * Usage: 
        s = solveSystem F
  * Inputs:
      * F, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, contains polynomials with complex
        coefficients
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note CorrectorTolerance: numerical homotopy tracking options, => ...,
        default value null, options for core functions of Numerical Algebraic
        Geometry
      * *note EndZoneFactor: numerical homotopy tracking options, => ...,
        default value null, options for core functions of Numerical Algebraic
        Geometry
      * *note gamma: numerical homotopy tracking options, => ..., default value
        null, options for core functions of Numerical Algebraic Geometry
      * *note InfinityThreshold: numerical homotopy tracking options, => ...,
        default value null, options for core functions of Numerical Algebraic
        Geometry
      * *note maxCorrSteps: numerical homotopy tracking options, => ...,
        default value null, options for core functions of Numerical Algebraic
        Geometry
      * *note Normalize: numerical homotopy tracking options, => ..., default
        value null, options for core functions of Numerical Algebraic Geometry
      * *note numberSuccessesBeforeIncrease: numerical homotopy tracking
        options, => ..., default value null, options for core functions of
        Numerical Algebraic Geometry
      * *note PostProcess: solveSystem_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmPostProcess=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,
        => ..., default value true, specifies whether to postprocess the
        solutions
      * *note Precision: numerical homotopy tracking options, => ..., default
        value null, options for core functions of Numerical Algebraic Geometry
      * *note Predictor: numerical homotopy tracking options, => ..., default
        value null, options for core functions of Numerical Algebraic Geometry
      * *note Projectivize: numerical homotopy tracking options, => ...,
        default value null, options for core functions of Numerical Algebraic
        Geometry
      * *note ResidualTolerance: numerical homotopy tracking options, => ...,
        default value null, options for core functions of Numerical Algebraic
        Geometry
      * *note SingularConditionNumber: numerical homotopy tracking options, =>
        ..., default value null, options for core functions of Numerical
        Algebraic Geometry
      * *note Software: Software, => ..., default value null, specify internal
        or external software
      * *note stepIncreaseFactor: numerical homotopy tracking options, => ...,
        default value null, options for core functions of Numerical Algebraic
        Geometry
      * *note tDegree: numerical homotopy tracking options, => ..., default
        value null, options for core functions of Numerical Algebraic Geometry
      * *note tStep: numerical homotopy tracking options, => ..., default value
        null, options for core functions of Numerical Algebraic Geometry
      * *note tStepMin: numerical homotopy tracking options, => ..., default
        value null, options for core functions of Numerical Algebraic Geometry
  * Outputs:
      * s, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, contains all complex solutions to
        the system F=0

Description
===========

Solve a system of polynomial equations using homotopy continuation methods.


+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = CC[x,y];                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : F = {x^2+y^2-1, x*y};                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : solveSystem F                                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = {{1, 8.30314e-21+4.44918e-20*ii}, {3.02251e-20+2.05294e-20*ii, -1},     |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     {-3.02251e-20-2.05294e-20*ii, 1}, {-1, -8.30314e-21-4.44918e-20*ii}}    |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
+----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : R = CC[x,y];                                                     |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : F = {x^2+y^2-1, x*y, x*(y+1)};                                   |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : solveSystem F                                                    |
|                                                                      |
|o6 = {{3.45943e-17+4.909e-17*ii, 1}, {5.40508e-17+2.78984e-17*ii, -1}}|
|                                                                      |
|o6 : List                                                             |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------+

The system is assumed to have finitely many solutions. If it is not square
(number of equations = number of variables), *note squareUp: squareUp, is
applied and solutions to the original system are then picked out from the
resulting (larger) set of solutions.

The output (produced by *note track: track_lpList_cmList_cmList_rp, with
default options) contains all *note points: (NAGtypes)AbstractPoint, obtained
at the end of homotopy paths when tracking starting at the *note
totalDegreeStartSystem: totalDegreeStartSystem_lpList_rp,. In particular, this
means that solving a system that has fewer than Bezout bound many solutions
will produce points that are not marked as regular. See *note track:
track_lpList_cmList_cmList_rp, for detailed examples.

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note solveSystem(List): solveSystem_lpList_rp, -- solve a system of
    polynomial equations
  * "solveSystem(PolySystem)"
