trackHomotopy(Homotopy,List) -- follow points along a homotopy
**************************************************************

  * Function: *note trackHomotopy: trackHomotopy_lpHomotopy_cmList_rp,
  * Usage: 
        trackHomotopy(H,S)
  * Inputs:
      * H, an instance of the type *note Homotopy: Homotopy,, 
      * S, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, start solutions
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note CorrectorTolerance: numerical homotopy tracking options, => ...,
        default value null, options for core functions of Numerical Algebraic
        Geometry
      * *note EndZoneFactor: numerical homotopy tracking options, => ...,
        default value null, options for core functions of Numerical Algebraic
        Geometry
      * Field => ..., default value null
      * *note InfinityThreshold: numerical homotopy tracking options, => ...,
        default value null, options for core functions of Numerical Algebraic
        Geometry
      * *note maxCorrSteps: numerical homotopy tracking options, => ...,
        default value null, options for core functions of Numerical Algebraic
        Geometry
      * *note NoOutput: numerical homotopy tracking options, => ..., default
        value null, options for core functions of Numerical Algebraic Geometry
      * *note numberSuccessesBeforeIncrease: numerical homotopy tracking
        options, => ..., default value null, options for core functions of
        Numerical Algebraic Geometry
      * *note Precision: numerical homotopy tracking options, => ..., default
        value null, options for core functions of Numerical Algebraic Geometry
      * *note Predictor: numerical homotopy tracking options, => ..., default
        value null, options for core functions of Numerical Algebraic Geometry
      * *note Software: numerical homotopy tracking options, => ..., default
        value null, options for core functions of Numerical Algebraic Geometry
      * *note stepIncreaseFactor: numerical homotopy tracking options, => ...,
        default value null, options for core functions of Numerical Algebraic
        Geometry
      * *note tStep: numerical homotopy tracking options, => ..., default value
        null, options for core functions of Numerical Algebraic Geometry
      * *note tStepMin: numerical homotopy tracking options, => ..., default
        value null, options for core functions of Numerical Algebraic Geometry
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,

Description
===========

This method implements homotopy continuation: it follows a given list S of
start solutions along a *note Homotopy: Homotopy, H.

Option *note Field: trackHomotopy_lpHomotopy_cmList_rp, (the default is *note
CC: (Macaulay2Doc)CC,, but one can imagine using *note RR: (Macaulay2Doc)RR,)
specifies which *note InexactFieldFamily: (Macaulay2Doc)InexactFieldFamily, to
use when adaptive precision is requested via Precision=>infinity. The rest are
a subset of *note numerical homotopy tracking options: numerical homotopy
tracking options,.

Caveat
======

Note for developers: the old implementation *note track:
track_lpList_cmList_cmList_rp, eventually will be replaced by a call to *note
trackHomotopy: trackHomotopy_lpHomotopy_cmList_rp,. Alternative ways for
calling (H could be a Sequence (a preSLP), Matrix, etc.) are deprecated and are
for debugging purposes only.

See also
========

  * *note GateHomotopy: gateHomotopy_lpGateMatrix_cmGateMatrix_cmInputGate_rp,
    -- homotopy implemented via straight line programs
  * *note segmentHomotopy: segmentHomotopy, -- a segment homotopy
  * *note AbstractPoint: (NAGtypes)AbstractPoint, -- a type used to store a
    point in complex space

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note trackHomotopy(Homotopy,List): trackHomotopy_lpHomotopy_cmList_rp, --
    follow points along a homotopy
  * "trackHomotopy(Matrix,List)"
  * "trackHomotopy(Sequence,List)"
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

